    "text": "<p>In the given circuit, diode <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is reverse biased, so it will not conduct but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> are forward biased, so they will conduct, hence corresponding equivalent circuit. For the given circuit is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/f26c2ab3-ada7-462b-bf4b-ba19fef8300c-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 227px;\" /></p><p>Now, the equivalent resistance of the circuit is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mn>515</mn></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Current through battery, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p>",
